Z||000000||grinthock||11-05-2001||07:08 PM||||Anyone know who sells a MITYVAC brake bleeder pump here in Canada?<P>------------------<BR> <A HREF="http://www.fieroworld.com" TARGET=_blank>www.fieroworld.com</A>  The place to go for Fiero INFO! <BR>Home of my 87 GT and 85 GT<BR>Justin C.<BR>Engineer, Designer and<BR>Technical Trainer for Nortel Networks Business Products.||||reg||1
Z||000001||theogre||11-05-2001||09:11 PM||||Did you try the parts stores? The Mityvac kits aren't always sold under that name. <P>What is called a MightyVac kit is usually the MightyVac plastic pump packaged by someone else with the bleeder stuff.<P>You can get a metal pump under the Actron brand.<P>you can also get the bleeder catch bottle separately If I remember right.<P><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/fullstaff.gif">  <FONT COLOR="blue"><I><B>11-Sept-01, The day the world as we knew it ended.</B></I></FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000002||jelly2m8||11-05-2001||11:11 PM||||Crappy tire carries them. You can usually find them in the HELP section with the misc fastners, special tools, etc. The crappy tire ones are made from plastic.<P> If you want a metal one try the snap-on dealer, but expect to pay at least double.||||reg||1
